(5587620, 807655, 30982, '<td valign="top">Classic and lovely, and perfect in B&amp;W.  You did a marvelous job with the lighting, particularly to bring out the hair and give depth to her face, with no hot spots, no glare, no harsh shadows.  VERY impressive!</td>', 'Classic and lovely, and perfect in B&W.  You did a marvelous job with the lighting, particularly to bring out the hair and give depth to her face, with no hot spots, no glare, no harsh shadows.  VERY impressive!', '2009-07-27 07:36:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5587621, 808077, 31637, '<td valign="top">Hello from the <u>Critique Club</u> <br/> <br/><b>PROS</b>: Technically sound portrait, doesn''t feel like a candid, or much of a setup, almost like a snapshot but also directed somewhat.  And I actually think its cropped pretty good. I don''t see any wasted area in the frame, and the exposure is good, a bit conservative maybe, could improve on contrast. <br/> <br/><b>CONS</b>: Overblown in areas. I think you had a window to work the shutter up a few stops for a better colorful contrast. Whites are dominating here. Some grays would help. <br/> <br/><b>VERDICT</b> <br/> <br/>Average at best, Id say slightly under-rated,  but nothing smiting. PM me if you have questions or answers about this critique.<br/> <br/>-Anton</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club  PROS: Technically sound portrait, doesn''t feel like a candid, or much of a setup, almost like a snapshot but also directed somewhat.  And I actually think its cropped pretty good. I don''t see any wasted area in the frame, and the exposure is good, a bit conservative maybe, could improve on contrast.  CONS: Overblown in areas. I think you had a window to work the shutter up a few stops for a better colorful contrast. Whites are dominating here. Some grays would help.  VERDICT  Average at best, Id say slightly under-rated,  but nothing smiting. PM me if you have questions or answers about this critique. -Anton', '2009-07-27 07:39:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5587622, 808320, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''ll disagree with the "too busy" but then you know me - I like stuff with depth and stuff to explore.  Lovely model (though I''ll echo that the lighting does tend to highlight her nose ring, which is OK if she''s good with that) and I really do like the lighting on her shoulder, her hair.  An interesting pose, too - nice use of curves, both hers and the props.  My only nit/suggestion would be that I can just see stuff in the background, in the upper left - either it needs to be completely blacked out (and yeah, editing rules and such - this is for non-DPC use) or not SO blacked out as to still be there enough to be a background.  Looks like you and Leo have a great time with these outings!</td>', 'I''ll disagree with the "too busy" but then you know me - I like stuff with depth and stuff to explore.  Lovely model (though I''ll echo that the lighting does tend to highlight her nose ring, which is OK if she''s good with that) and I really do like the lighting on her shoulder, her hair.  An interesting pose, too - nice use of curves, both hers and the props.  My only nit/suggestion would be that I can just see stuff in the background, in the upper left - either it needs to be completely blacked out (and yeah, editing rules and such - this is for non-DPC use) or not SO blacked out as to still be there enough to be a background.  Looks like you and Leo have a great time with these outings!', '2009-07-27 07:39:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5587623, 808190, 30982, '<td valign="top">I quite like this one, Brian - I remember it well from voting.  His blue eyes are captivating and he has a very honest face.  Very nice choice of composition - I like the slight slope to the shot - suits the way he''s looking well.  Given that, I''d like to see a wee bit more of the shoulder if possible, to give it just a bit more of a base.  It has that now, but almost looks accidental rather than intentional.  And I really like the way the light is hitting his hair in the back.</td>', 'I quite like this one, Brian - I remember it well from voting.  His blue eyes are captivating and he has a very honest face.  Very nice choice of composition - I like the slight slope to the shot - suits the way he''s looking well.  Given that, I''d like to see a wee bit more of the shoulder if possible, to give it just a bit more of a base.  It has that now, but almost looks accidental rather than intentional.  And I really like the way the light is hitting his hair in the back.', '2009-07-27 07:42:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5587624, 808084, 30982, '<td valign="top">Perhaps a bit soft and a bit bright, but I recall when voting that I liked the ethereal feel of it, which is different given it is a treatment used more often with females than males.  For a self portrait I think it''s a good take (I''m assuming it''s a self-portrait!) because for me it''s wickedly hard to get one''s self in focus.  I know others manage to pull it off, but I have no idea how.  I also checked out your outtakes - I think I prefer the direct eye contact in the B&amp;W outtake, though that one too needed a bit more focus to really work well.</td>', 'Perhaps a bit soft and a bit bright, but I recall when voting that I liked the ethereal feel of it, which is different given it is a treatment used more often with females than males.  For a self portrait I think it''s a good take (I''m assuming it''s a self-portrait!) because for me it''s wickedly hard to get one''s self in focus.  I know others manage to pull it off, but I have no idea how.  I also checked out your outtakes - I think I prefer the direct eye contact in the B&W outtake, though that one too needed a bit more focus to really work well.', '2009-07-27 07:44:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5587625, 808072, 106349, '<td valign="top">This was one of my highest votes! It''s a great portrait; detail is riveting.</td>', 'This was one of my highest votes! It''s a great portrait; detail is riveting.', '2009-07-27 07:49:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5587626, 808171, 30982, '<td valign="top">Darn fine job with the focus for a self portrait!  I''ve never been able to figure that out.  Good job with the light - it feels a bit like window light (though I suspect it''s an actual light) and you''ve done well to avoid hot spots.  I just checked the comments and a couple others have pointed out what I was going to say next - the hands are entirely too clean!  :-)  The flour on the face looks too "posed", especially given how clean the hands and arms are.  Still, as I said I''m very impressed with the focus and a very good idea for the challenge!</td>', 'Darn fine job with the focus for a self portrait!  I''ve never been able to figure that out.  Good job with the light - it feels a bit like window light (though I suspect it''s an actual light) and you''ve done well to avoid hot spots.  I just checked the comments and a couple others have pointed out what I was going to say next - the hands are entirely too clean!  :-)  The flour on the face looks too "posed", especially given how clean the hands and arms are.  Still, as I said I''m very impressed with the focus and a very good idea for the challenge!', '2009-07-27 07:49:39.000000', NULL, 0),
