(5587760, 807643, 49954, '<td valign="top">[quote]My worry is that in an effort to keep the focus squarely on the eyes I have over-softened the rest. No doubt folks will let me know![/quote]<br/> <br/>Appears they DID let you know and know well!  WONDERFUL SHOT!</td>', '[quote]My worry is that in an effort to keep the focus squarely on the eyes I have over-softened the rest. No doubt folks will let me know![/quote] Appears they DID let you know and know well!  WONDERFUL SHOT!', '2009-07-27 11:00:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5587761, 808199, 70369, '<td valign="top">I wondered about a maternity shot for this &amp; if anyone would submit one.. To me, I thought the voters would DNMC it because obviously there''s technically a child there, and DP voters are VERY technical. If I had voted, I wouldn''t have cared and I would have voted on the merit of the image only. <br/>In that regards, I think the position is a nice one. I don''t really care for the duotone you chose. I think it''s a bit harsh for a subject that is soft &amp; gentle. I would have preferred something very subtle. b &amp; w with maybe just a touch of sepia. I also would have chosen to blur out more of the background.. it''s a busy background and I think it takes away from your subject. There''s a cool tutorial on using channels and the brush tool to blur out the entire image and only paint back in the area you want to be sharp. It gives you a lens baby effect. I think this image would have been perfect for that. Just MHO. :-)</td>', 'I wondered about a maternity shot for this & if anyone would submit one.. To me, I thought the voters would DNMC it because obviously there''s technically a child there, and DP voters are VERY technical. If I had voted, I wouldn''t have cared and I would have voted on the merit of the image only. In that regards, I think the position is a nice one. I don''t really care for the duotone you chose. I think it''s a bit harsh for a subject that is soft & gentle. I would have preferred something very subtle. b & w with maybe just a touch of sepia. I also would have chosen to blur out more of the background.. it''s a busy background and I think it takes away from your subject. There''s a cool tutorial on using channels and the brush tool to blur out the entire image and only paint back in the area you want to be sharp. It gives you a lens baby effect. I think this image would have been perfect for that. Just MHO. :-)', '2009-07-27 11:00:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5587762, 807643, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful photo!  Love the lighting - soft and perfect.  Congrats on the ribbon and on your new PB!</td>', 'This is a beautiful photo!  Love the lighting - soft and perfect.  Congrats on the ribbon and on your new PB!', '2009-07-27 11:00:53.000000', NULL, 0),
